Patch 2020: the vertex-program texture binding path records the 16-bit colour formats.

It only recorded formats 0x81/85/8B/86-88/9A; a unit set to any other format (A1R5G5B5, A4R4G4B4, R5G6B5, R5G5B5A1, D1R5G5B5,
D8R8G8B8) kept the previous texture, so the character-select labels were drawn with the wrong texture. The layout and decode code
already handles these formats. RSX_TEX_FMT16=0 restores the old behaviour. Diagnostics: TEX_DDS_OFF, ATLAS_VTX, TEXSKIP_DBG.

Re-fitted for v0.19.0: The list of recorded formats merged with v0.19.0's (#635).

